From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:54:12 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nouveau: attach the side by side (full) timing to DP
 connectors

The "side by side full timing" connector property chooses how an HDMI
side by side (full) mode is timed. It was attached to HDMI connectors
only, while nouveau also drives HDMI through DisplayPort connectors with a
DP++ adaptor (the connector's TMDS encoder, found by DDC), where the same
modes are offered. Attach it to the DisplayPort connectors that allow
stereo too. The "HDMI 3D metadata" property stays off: nouveau's vendor
InfoFrame registers take PB0 to PB6 only.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.c | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.c
index 32e8df40f..d2b908a49 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nouveau_connector.c
@@ -1519,10 +1519,14 @@ nouveau_connector_create(struct drm_device *dev, int index)
 		connector->stereo_allowed = true;
 
 	/*
-	 * The vendor InfoFrame registers take PB0 to PB6 only, so the 3D
-	 * metadata, which starts at PB6 or PB7, cannot be sent.
+	 * HDMI is driven through HDMI connectors, and through DisplayPort ones
+	 * with a DP++ adaptor, the TMDS encoder found by DDC. The vendor
+	 * InfoFrame registers take PB0 to PB6 only, so the 3D metadata, which
+	 * starts at PB6 or PB7, cannot be sent.
 	 */
-	if (connector->stereo_allowed && type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA)
+	if (connector->stereo_allowed &&
+	    (type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA ||
+	     type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_DisplayPort))
 		drm_connector_attach_sbs_full_timing_property(connector);
 
 	/* defaults, will get overridden in detect() */
